The attached image (Fig. 4) demonstrates the active transport of Nano-11 nanoparticles by APCs to the draining lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots show Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peaking in number at day 2, with migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) comprising the largest fraction (60-80%) of these Nano-11-positive cells. MigDCs also exhibit significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) for Nano-11 compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDCs) and macrophages/monocytes (Mo/MΦ), indicating more efficient uptake per cell. This suggests Nano-11 effectively targets immunopotentiating MigDCs in vivo.